WEBVTT

00:00:17.000 --> 00:00:18.560
Fluffy...

00:00:22.110 --> 00:00:25.620
Fluffy and warm...

00:00:30.910 --> 00:00:32.970
Fluffy...

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:26.140
Shower...

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:33.300
Shower...

00:02:33.650 --> 00:02:35.210
Shower...

00:02:39.620 --> 00:02:40.380
Hmm?

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:45.280
Huh?

00:03:00.910 --> 00:03:05.910
<b>Her Assistant Knows Not Her Highness's Heart.</b>

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:12.330
What's wrong, Your Highness?

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:16.120
Nothing...

00:03:16.120 --> 00:03:19.050
But you look like something's bothering you.

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:20.940
<i>I can't tell him.</i>

00:03:21.330 --> 00:03:25.440
<i>I can't tell him that the sweater 
he got me ended up like that...</i>

00:03:25.920 --> 00:03:27.810
<i>I was trying not to let it get ruined.</i>

00:03:29.700 --> 00:03:31.770
<i>Did I do something?</i>

00:03:34.920 --> 00:03:38.630
<i>It seems like she doesn't 
even want to look at me...</i>

00:03:42.120 --> 00:03:45.120
I wonder if I did something again...

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:45.120
Hey! Hey! Hey!

00:03:45.630 --> 00:03:51.080
I think you're just being too self-conscious.

00:03:51.290 --> 00:03:54.120
But she sighed after looking at me!

00:03:54.120 --> 00:03:56.670
You're being pretty mean again, today!

00:03:57.000 --> 00:03:59.570
And you're being annoying again.

00:03:59.570 --> 00:04:03.600
<i>He's a bit upset because 
his new book didn't arrive.</i>

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:07.180
<i>I need to do something about this...</i>

00:04:08.230 --> 00:04:10.450
U-Um, Your Highness...

00:04:13.630 --> 00:04:16.480
<i>Half of it is still the 
original sweater, so...</i>

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:19.560
<i>I might be able to secretly fix it, if I try.</i>

00:04:19.560 --> 00:04:21.820
<i>I don't really know how to knit,</i>

00:04:22.050 --> 00:04:26.110
<i>but if I just put the threads together, 
I might be able to figure it out.</i>

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:28.050
<i>I might be able to fix this.</i>

00:04:28.050 --> 00:04:29.510
U-Um, Your Highness.

00:04:38.640 --> 00:04:40.670
<i>I can't fix this!</i>

00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:41.760
<i>A pile of yarn.</i>

00:04:43.320 --> 00:04:45.480
Adrammelech...

00:04:45.480 --> 00:04:49.100
Oh, my. What's wrong, Your Highness?

00:04:49.310 --> 00:04:53.510
I'm sorry for disturbing you 
at this hour, but my sweater...

00:04:53.510 --> 00:04:54.840
My sweater...

00:04:54.840 --> 00:04:56.190
Your sweater?

00:04:57.320 --> 00:04:58.880
My sweater...

00:04:58.880 --> 00:05:00.400
<i>At least it was.</i>

00:05:00.640 --> 00:05:02.700
Well, this is quite the mess.

00:05:02.700 --> 00:05:04.390
Can it be fixed?!

00:05:04.390 --> 00:05:06.080
Let's see...

00:05:06.080 --> 00:05:10.330
This is 100% Alpaca fur. Nice and silky.

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:16.250
<i>Though this is one of the more reasonable 
items in Her Highness' possession.</i>

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:20.520
Well, someone picked it out for me after 
thinking about how it'd feel on the skin.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:22.640
You didn't pick it out yourself?

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:24.450
Mullin gave it to me.

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:27.600
Oh, my. That means he spent quite 
a bit of money on it, then.

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:29.020
Good for him.

00:05:29.020 --> 00:05:30.720
What was the occasion for the gift?

00:05:31.230 --> 00:05:34.250
He didn't want me to sleep naked?

00:05:34.670 --> 00:05:36.060
What do you mean?

00:05:36.060 --> 00:05:37.640
<i>Watch episode one for more details.</i>

00:05:37.970 --> 00:05:40.870
Well, it's okay. 
You're in luck, Your Highness.

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:43.080
These threads are all linked together,

00:05:43.080 --> 00:05:44.850
so I think I can fix it up pretty well.

00:05:44.850 --> 00:05:46.450
R-Really?!

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:48.960
If I try to put the knitting on 
this sweater through a machine,

00:05:46.450 --> 00:05:52.100
I don't really understand, 
but you can fix it, right?!

00:05:48.960 --> 00:05:52.100
it'll end up cutting the yarn short, 
so it might be difficult to fix, but...

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:52.860
Yes.

00:05:53.310 --> 00:05:54.830
I'm glad...

00:05:56.020 --> 00:05:59.040
Quite an important sweater, huh?

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:01.290
Don't worry about it.

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:03.190
I'll deliver it to you by tomorrow morning.

00:06:03.190 --> 00:06:05.600
Tell me what the design was for the sweater.

00:06:05.600 --> 00:06:06.640
Thank—

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:08.350
Wait, I'll come and get it myself.

00:06:08.350 --> 00:06:10.260
It's fine, Your Highness.

00:06:10.750 --> 00:06:13.430
I want to keep this a secret from Mullin.

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:15.710
Mullin gave it to me,

00:06:15.710 --> 00:06:19.600
and I feel so bad it ended up like this.

00:06:20.100 --> 00:06:22.620
I understand. I'll fix it right up.

00:06:22.620 --> 00:06:24.390
So don't worry, and get to sleep.

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:27.210
Make sure you wear something, naked lady.

00:06:27.210 --> 00:06:28.090
Okay.

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:31.760
Thank you, again.

00:06:31.760 --> 00:06:33.060
Good night.

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:39.310
Now, then...

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:41.620
Where were my knitting needles...

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:45.800
She was so worried...

00:06:47.410 --> 00:06:49.310
She wants to get it fixed 
so she can still wear it...

00:06:50.630 --> 00:06:55.420
I think if I told Mullin, 
he'd actually be happy to hear it.

00:07:05.310 --> 00:07:06.980
<i>I thought all night,</i>

00:07:06.980 --> 00:07:09.860
<i>but I couldn't figure out why 
Her Highness was so down.</i>

00:07:10.640 --> 00:07:12.470
<i>I should trying asking her one more time.</i>

00:07:13.440 --> 00:07:14.660
Oh, Your Highness.

00:07:15.400 --> 00:07:16.990
Good morning.

00:07:16.990 --> 00:07:19.840
Did I do something yesterday—

00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:19.840
Mullin.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:25.130
Let's work hard, like always.

00:07:30.730 --> 00:07:33.780
<i>Maybe I really am self-conscious?</i>

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:49.440
It was so warm, I was
tired that entire meeting.

00:07:51.120 --> 00:07:52.860
Well, it is spring.

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:55.910
Yeah, it's the season where you have 
to fend of being sleepy all the time.

00:07:56.810 --> 00:07:59.720
Yeah, it really is the season... for pollen.

00:07:59.720 --> 00:08:01.940
Don't you feel bad for me?

00:08:01.940 --> 00:08:03.750
Bell, make me feel better.

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:05.090
If you want to combat the pollen,

00:08:05.090 --> 00:08:08.060
then this mask that Dantalion 
gave me is the best you can do!

00:08:10.160 --> 00:08:13.440
This pollen is terrible!

00:08:13.440 --> 00:08:15.460
I feel bad for him.

00:08:16.170 --> 00:08:19.390
I want to ask who he is,
but it's easy to guess.

00:08:20.070 --> 00:08:23.460
Did the Accounting Department already have 
their flower-viewing party for the year?

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:25.350
Yeah, we did, the other day.

00:08:25.350 --> 00:08:27.400
Oh, that's pretty nice.

00:08:27.650 --> 00:08:30.860
That makes sense. Everyone goes 
with their respective departments.

00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:33.360
Not everyone goes, though.

00:08:33.950 --> 00:08:38.360
Astaroth-sama, you didn't use the opportunity 
to sexually harass anyone, did you?

00:08:38.360 --> 00:08:39.710
I didn't.

00:08:39.710 --> 00:08:41.540
Actually, I was cut off 
alone from everyone else,

00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:43.500
for some reason I don't understand.

00:08:44.310 --> 00:08:46.210
Sacchan! Hey, Sacchan!

00:08:46.640 --> 00:08:49.360
Hey! Is there even a 
reason for me to be here?

00:08:49.360 --> 00:08:50.670
Just being careful.

00:08:50.940 --> 00:08:52.660
<i>She doesn't trust him at all...</i>

00:08:52.660 --> 00:08:55.630
<i>Preventing something before it happens.</i>

00:08:56.060 --> 00:08:58.590
You should have let me join you.

00:08:58.960 --> 00:09:01.090
You went with the Succubus 
Division this year, too, right?

00:09:01.090 --> 00:09:01.870
Yes.

00:09:01.870 --> 00:09:02.600
What?!

00:09:02.840 --> 00:09:03.870
<i>Wow.</i>

00:09:03.870 --> 00:09:05.560
<i>I bet that was fun.</i>

00:09:06.770 --> 00:09:09.060
<b>The Succubus Division &
Apparel and Design
Department in his mind</b>

00:09:09.520 --> 00:09:10.400
Sorry, it wasn't like that.

00:09:10.890 --> 00:09:13.800
We had a fried chicken eating contest.

00:09:13.800 --> 00:09:15.610
Carnivorously aggressive women!

00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:20.100
First place this year was a set of 
high-end lingerie that cost 100,000 yen.

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:22.180
They were all in a frenzy.

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:23.540
A hundred thousand yen?!

00:09:23.540 --> 00:09:25.930
You mean to wear for work, 
when they need to get things done?

00:09:26.640 --> 00:09:28.220
I love that idea.

00:09:28.220 --> 00:09:29.770
For at-home use, of course.

00:09:29.770 --> 00:09:34.360
They use a lot more innocent and 
cheap lingerie for their work.

00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:35.220
<i>Shameless.</i>

00:09:35.440 --> 00:09:39.220
You and Morrigan seem to be quite close.

00:09:39.220 --> 00:09:40.510
Not really surprising, though.

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:44.680
Well, at first, we were 
just work acquaintances.

00:09:41.100 --> 00:09:44.680
<b>Seduction Department,
Succubus Section Chief
Morrigan</b>

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:47.850
You know the part you hold on a drumstick?

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:52.270
<b>This is called
the drumstick</b>

00:09:47.640 --> 00:09:52.270
<b>This thing</b>

00:09:47.850 --> 00:09:49.700
Y-Yeah?

00:09:49.700 --> 00:09:52.270
Well, there was this 
flower-viewing party years ago...

00:09:54.130 --> 00:09:57.950
Morrigan was using them as maracas, 
and was dancing around with them.

00:09:58.880 --> 00:10:00.270
You go, Morrigan-sama!

00:10:00.270 --> 00:10:02.530
You're so cool, chief!

00:10:03.910 --> 00:10:07.310
That's when I thought I could become 
good friends with this girl.

00:10:07.310 --> 00:10:09.370
So I decided to talk to her.

00:10:09.590 --> 00:10:13.440
And she didn't even have 
a drop of alcohol in her.

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:14.800
Pretty amazing, huh?

00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:15.710
Mambo!

00:10:15.710 --> 00:10:17.290
I wish you hadn't told me that story!

00:10:17.470 --> 00:10:19.470
<b>*After the chief was done dancing, she gobbled up her maracas</b>

00:10:20.240 --> 00:10:23.430
Flower-viewing sounds fun.

00:10:23.950 --> 00:10:27.290
Your office doesn't have 
that yearly ritual, huh?

00:10:27.290 --> 00:10:31.800
I'm worried that anyone under me wouldn't be 
able to relax around me at an event like that.

00:10:31.800 --> 00:10:34.200
That's not true at all!

00:10:34.200 --> 00:10:36.280
I never knew, though.

00:10:36.280 --> 00:10:38.690
I won't tell you to do it,

00:10:38.690 --> 00:10:42.530
but it's a convenient way to break the ice.

00:10:42.780 --> 00:10:46.760
Also, I've never gone flower-viewing before,

00:10:46.760 --> 00:10:48.620
so I'm not sure what to do.

00:10:48.840 --> 00:10:51.080
What, Bell?! You've never gone before?!

00:10:51.360 --> 00:10:52.600
When I was younger

00:10:52.600 --> 00:10:57.410
I would have tea and look at the seasonal flowers in the mansion garden, but...

00:10:57.410 --> 00:10:59.400
I guess you could call that flower-viewing,

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:00.790
but it's not quite right.

00:11:00.790 --> 00:11:01.930
<i>Very elegant.</i>

00:11:02.180 --> 00:11:05.010
Well, Your Highness, would you like 
to try having a flower-viewing party?

00:11:05.200 --> 00:11:06.070
Huh?

00:11:06.070 --> 00:11:08.240
We could invite people from 
other departments, too.

00:11:08.240 --> 00:11:10.710
I'm sure it'd be hard for everyone 
to make plans out of the blue,

00:11:10.710 --> 00:11:13.610
so we could even do it during lunchtime 
and eat together, or something.

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:15.270
That sounds good.

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:18.110
The Underworld Central Park 
is pretty close, too.

00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:19.860
I want to go, too.

00:11:19.860 --> 00:11:21.090
Count me in.

00:11:21.090 --> 00:11:22.610
Me, too, then!

00:11:22.610 --> 00:11:25.840
I'm not sure what my boss will do,

00:11:25.840 --> 00:11:26.860
so I'll be going.

00:11:27.540 --> 00:11:28.880
Are you sure?

00:11:28.880 --> 00:11:29.650
Yes.

00:11:31.000 --> 00:11:33.080
Thank you very much!

00:11:33.430 --> 00:11:36.080
<i>She's so cute!</i>

00:11:36.080 --> 00:11:38.550
<i>A smile you want to protect.</i>

00:11:39.100 --> 00:11:41.370
We'll need to prepare lunch.

00:11:41.760 --> 00:11:43.780
There will be seven here...

00:11:43.780 --> 00:11:47.340
I can ask Bro and Gocchin, too. 
That makes nine.

00:11:47.340 --> 00:11:47.890
Oh.

00:11:48.410 --> 00:11:51.360
I'm sure you'll be going, too, 
Eurynome-san, so that makes ten.

00:11:51.360 --> 00:11:53.120
You did well to realize.

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:56.020
<i>There will be glasses where 
ever there is Dantalion-love.</i>

00:11:56.490 --> 00:11:58.870
We could just do a potluck.

00:11:58.870 --> 00:12:00.230
Everyone has to bring one item.

00:12:00.230 --> 00:12:03.520
You can make something, buy something, 
or just bring something you like.

00:12:03.520 --> 00:12:05.330
You could bring KFC,

00:12:05.330 --> 00:12:08.320
a fancy side-dish from a store, or even 
rice balls from the convenience store.

00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:09.840
That's a great idea!

00:12:09.840 --> 00:12:13.750
I love super-casual gatherings like that.

00:12:14.740 --> 00:12:17.600
I've never had KFC before!

00:12:17.600 --> 00:12:18.740
Seriously?!

00:12:18.740 --> 00:12:21.600
KFC is really good! KFC!

00:12:21.600 --> 00:12:23.090
Shut up.

00:12:23.530 --> 00:12:26.240
Okay, well let's all meet there at lunch.

00:12:26.240 --> 00:12:27.550
Right!

00:12:29.210 --> 00:12:34.350
<i>And then lunch came upon the 
Underworld Central Park.</i>

00:12:36.540 --> 00:12:37.630
It's beautiful here.

00:12:37.630 --> 00:12:39.440
Blossoms are in full bloom.

00:12:39.850 --> 00:12:42.400
Your Highness, over here!

00:12:42.680 --> 00:12:45.130
Okay, come over!

00:12:45.130 --> 00:12:47.870
Everyone put out what you brought!

00:12:47.870 --> 00:12:48.870
Okay!

00:12:50.100 --> 00:12:52.620
<i>And a good 90% was KFC.</i>

00:12:53.240 --> 00:12:56.390
What... is the meaning of this?

00:12:56.390 --> 00:12:59.070
You can't mean everyone brought chicken...

00:12:59.070 --> 00:13:01.890
I thought Her Highness would be happy...

00:13:01.890 --> 00:13:03.610
I got a bucket...

00:13:04.350 --> 00:13:07.610
This isn't a flower-viewing 
party... It's a KFC party.

00:13:07.610 --> 00:13:10.970
I think even Her Highness isn't 
going to want this much...

00:13:14.060 --> 00:13:15.050
This is good!

00:13:15.050 --> 00:13:16.600
What is this?!

00:13:16.600 --> 00:13:17.580
It is, isn't it?

00:13:17.580 --> 00:13:19.790
I love it, too!

00:13:19.790 --> 00:13:22.690
<i>Well, at least she's happy.</i>

00:13:25.490 --> 00:13:28.170
KFC is really good!

00:13:28.170 --> 00:13:29.320
Yeah!

00:13:30.870 --> 00:13:33.840
I remember in middle school, there was a 
girl who went to put on some lip gloss,

00:13:33.840 --> 00:13:37.420
and I asked her if she went to get 
some chicken, and she got mad at me...

00:13:41.660 --> 00:13:44.460
The cookies you made are great, Bro!

00:13:44.460 --> 00:13:46.930
Thank you.
There's more.

00:13:44.460 --> 00:13:46.930
<b>Munch</b>

00:13:45.530 --> 00:13:46.450
Oh, yeah.

00:13:47.310 --> 00:13:50.050
<i>Gocchin-san likes cookies, doesn't she?</i>

00:13:50.920 --> 00:13:53.720
I guess she's scared, 
and can't ask him for any.

00:13:54.360 --> 00:13:57.290
Gocchin-san, Bro's cookies are pretty good.

00:13:57.920 --> 00:14:01.800
Th-Thank y-you!

00:14:01.800 --> 00:14:04.610
Good for you, Belphegor-sama.

00:14:04.920 --> 00:14:05.720
Yeah...

00:14:06.580 --> 00:14:09.320
<i>Azazel-sama's handmade cookies...</i>

00:14:11.450 --> 00:14:12.780
They're great, aren't they?

00:14:14.780 --> 00:14:15.830
Gocchin!

00:14:14.780 --> 00:14:16.640
Belphegor-sama!

00:14:16.640 --> 00:14:18.140
<i>Too much joy.</i>

00:14:19.330 --> 00:14:21.210
Oh, Nisroch!

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:23.420
<b>Former Principality, Demon
Nisroch</b>

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:23.420
<b>Former Guard of Eden's
"Forbidden Fruit"</b>

00:14:21.210 --> 00:14:23.420
Thanks for coming.

00:14:23.760 --> 00:14:26.350
I thought we needed a bit 
more than just fried chicken.

00:14:26.350 --> 00:14:29.000
Hopefully you can do something quick.

00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:30.340
If it's for the Miss...

00:14:33.350 --> 00:14:35.770
<i>And, of course, his clothes will fly off.</i>

00:14:38.980 --> 00:14:41.230
Wh-What's his deal?!

00:14:41.230 --> 00:14:43.080
Showy, as always.

00:14:43.080 --> 00:14:44.360
Th-Thanks.

00:14:44.360 --> 00:14:46.260
So this is normal?!

00:14:51.680 --> 00:14:53.710
It was nice she got the cookie.

00:14:55.290 --> 00:14:57.950
So where's Dantalion-san and the others?

00:14:59.930 --> 00:15:00.870
<i>He's reading...</i>

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:03.920
<i>He's jumping around in the gas mask...</i>

00:15:01.420 --> 00:15:05.350
Watching all the flower!

00:15:03.920 --> 00:15:05.350
<i>And she's lying in the grass.</i>

00:15:06.010 --> 00:15:07.530
<i>It must be some kind of cult.</i>

00:15:08.180 --> 00:15:10.430
<i>Idolatry.</i>

00:15:11.080 --> 00:15:14.640
<i>It's kind of creepy that 
Eurynome-san is being all quiet.</i>

00:15:14.640 --> 00:15:17.160
"Dantalion-love in the cherry blossoms!

00:15:17.160 --> 00:15:20.860
It's like an angel in a dream 
that's all this stuff!"

00:15:20.860 --> 00:15:23.400
<i>I thought that's how she'd be, but...</i>

00:15:23.930 --> 00:15:26.830
They say that you get bored of a 
beautiful girl or guy right away,

00:15:30.190 --> 00:15:34.520
but things that are truly 
beautiful, you can watch forever.

00:15:35.060 --> 00:15:38.590
Those that get bored aren't 
really seeing true beauty.

00:15:39.080 --> 00:15:40.430
I pity them.

00:15:40.430 --> 00:15:41.960
Y-You think so?

00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:43.540
<i>Enlightenment-nome-san.</i>

00:15:45.720 --> 00:15:48.800
<i>Eurynome-san is pretty amazing.</i>

00:15:48.800 --> 00:15:50.290
<i>It's nice that she's unique,</i>

00:15:50.290 --> 00:15:52.260
<i>but I'm not sure I'd want 
to be unique in that way.</i>

00:15:56.950 --> 00:15:58.750
It's really pretty.

00:15:59.610 --> 00:16:01.550
Y-Yeah.

00:16:01.550 --> 00:16:02.900
I know, right?!

00:16:02.900 --> 00:16:05.490
<i>Man, I could watch her forever.</i>

00:16:05.960 --> 00:16:08.360
I'm going to end up just like Eurynome-san.

00:16:08.790 --> 00:16:11.330
She's so innocent.

00:16:11.330 --> 00:16:14.080
I was like that once.

00:16:18.940 --> 00:16:22.000
It looks like you can catch the 
petals, but you can't, huh?

00:16:22.200 --> 00:16:27.640
They say you'll end up happy if you can 
catch a petal before it hits the ground.

00:16:27.640 --> 00:16:29.460
Making a wish, huh?

00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:31.340
Something like that.

00:16:31.340 --> 00:16:33.370
Why don't you give it a try, Sacchan?

00:16:33.370 --> 00:16:35.470
Huh? Why me?

00:16:35.840 --> 00:16:39.100
Well, you're always looking after me,

00:16:39.100 --> 00:16:41.470
so I'm sure any happiness is 
leaving you behind, by now.

00:16:41.470 --> 00:16:44.940
So, at the very least, you could try making 
a wish on a cherry blossom.

00:16:44.940 --> 00:16:45.940
Uh...

00:16:46.660 --> 00:16:50.260
<i>That's not really something 
I think or feel, but...</i>

00:16:50.760 --> 00:16:53.710
<i>It's not like I don't like 
taking care of him...</i>

00:16:54.180 --> 00:16:54.900
<i>What?!</i>

00:16:54.900 --> 00:16:56.720
<i>What was I thinking just now?!</i>

00:16:56.720 --> 00:16:57.700
<i>I don't hate it?</i>

00:16:57.700 --> 00:16:59.220
<i>Of course I do!</i>

00:16:59.220 --> 00:17:01.100
<i>I end up getting my work interrupted.</i>

00:17:01.100 --> 00:17:03.370
<i>He ends up wasting so much of my time!</i>

00:17:03.700 --> 00:17:06.470
<i>Why do I not hate it?</i>

00:17:09.120 --> 00:17:11.280
Sacchan, what's wrong?

00:17:11.280 --> 00:17:12.730
Nothing!

00:17:15.440 --> 00:17:16.400
All right...

00:17:16.400 --> 00:17:17.840
I'm going to get that one!

00:17:19.380 --> 00:17:20.390
Wait!

00:17:22.070 --> 00:17:23.170
Your Highness?!

00:17:23.170 --> 00:17:24.500
<i>Dumb and cute.</i>

00:17:33.540 --> 00:17:35.480
I can't get any of these...

00:17:35.950 --> 00:17:38.000
<i>This is rather difficult...</i>

00:17:42.320 --> 00:17:46.150
<i>A warm spring wind that engulfs the body.</i>

00:17:48.570 --> 00:17:50.190
<i>It's pretty out here,</i>

00:17:50.190 --> 00:17:53.840
<i>but kind of lonely, sad...</i>

00:17:54.280 --> 00:17:55.580
<i>Ephemeral...</i>

00:17:56.270 --> 00:17:57.840
Oh, I got lucky!

00:17:57.840 --> 00:17:58.770
I got one!

00:17:58.770 --> 00:18:00.300
Your Highness, did you see?!

00:18:02.400 --> 00:18:03.280
Your Highness?

00:18:06.140 --> 00:18:09.440
<i>It feels like this moment could 
be taken away at any time.</i>

00:18:11.800 --> 00:18:12.700
Your Highness!

00:18:13.580 --> 00:18:14.740
What is it?

00:18:15.930 --> 00:18:18.590
You scared me!

00:18:18.590 --> 00:18:19.740
Why?

00:18:21.520 --> 00:18:23.650
Uh, well...

00:18:24.180 --> 00:18:26.830
I thought you went missing...

00:18:29.520 --> 00:18:31.830
I-I see...

00:18:32.870 --> 00:18:34.800
<i>Why am I so embarrassed?</i>

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:37.130
<i>They're both oblivious.</i>

00:18:38.470 --> 00:18:40.460
Hey! You're hiding again.

00:18:40.460 --> 00:18:41.270
Your Highness!

00:18:41.270 --> 00:18:42.600
B-But...

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:43.990
Your Highness!

00:18:43.990 --> 00:18:46.750
Hey, stop chasing me!

00:18:46.750 --> 00:18:48.440
Wait!

00:18:47.250 --> 00:18:50.840
<i>How are those creatures so adorable?</i>

00:18:50.840 --> 00:18:52.460
<i>They're giving me a headache.</i>

00:19:04.760 --> 00:19:06.020
<i>It's already spring...</i>

00:19:08.370 --> 00:19:10.190
<i>Today's just like every other day so far.</i>

00:19:10.840 --> 00:19:11.870
<i>But...</i>

00:19:11.870 --> 00:19:13.440
<i>beginnings are always different.</i>

00:19:13.440 --> 00:19:16.380
Are you okay?

00:19:22.500 --> 00:19:24.220
<i>Even if you think things are the same,</i>

00:19:24.930 --> 00:19:28.180
<i>maybe, somewhere, they're a little different.</i>

00:19:43.210 --> 00:19:44.620
This is really fun.

00:19:45.390 --> 00:19:48.360
I couldn't catch a petal, though.

00:19:50.240 --> 00:19:52.240
Oh, I know, Your Highness.

00:19:52.240 --> 00:19:53.530
Give me your hand.

00:19:53.530 --> 00:19:54.130
Huh?

00:19:55.250 --> 00:19:57.080
I'll give this to you.

00:19:59.920 --> 00:20:01.810
I caught it a little bit ago.

00:20:01.810 --> 00:20:03.480
Th-This is yours?

00:20:03.480 --> 00:20:06.960
Oh, I guess you have to catch one 
yourself for it to mean something.

00:20:11.670 --> 00:20:13.390
Thank you.

00:20:18.040 --> 00:20:22.280
Sitting outside, eating, while looking at the 
cherry blossoms and talking with everyone...

00:20:22.280 --> 00:20:25.780
I never knew it could be so much fun.

00:20:27.140 --> 00:20:29.380
Flower-viewing is wonderful.

00:20:30.240 --> 00:20:33.720
Makes you not want to go back to work.

00:20:33.720 --> 00:20:35.250
You have to go back!

00:20:35.250 --> 00:20:37.000
I know that.

00:20:37.280 --> 00:20:40.530
We have to get back soon!

00:20:40.530 --> 00:20:42.220
Lunch'll be over soon!

00:20:42.920 --> 00:20:43.980
Okay!

00:20:47.750 --> 00:20:51.840
We should go flower-viewing with 
everyone from the office, too.

00:20:51.840 --> 00:20:52.470
Huh?

00:20:53.930 --> 00:20:56.770
Let's come again before 
all the blossoms fall.

00:20:59.200 --> 00:20:59.970
Yeah.

00:21:05.690 --> 00:21:10.410
<i>I'm sure she still can't put words to 
the emotions she's feeling right now.</i>

00:21:12.980 --> 00:21:14.030
Mullin!

00:21:14.030 --> 00:21:16.180
Sorry, I'll help!

00:21:16.870 --> 00:21:21.680
<i>But maybe someday, she will.</i>

00:21:24.560 --> 00:21:30.660
<i>This is the story of how she 
comes to name those feelings.</i>

00:21:33.060 --> 00:21:40.060
<b>The Name of That Feeling Is...</b>

00:23:10.990 --> 00:23:13.450
<b>A few days later...</b>

00:23:14.850 --> 00:23:16.080
Hold on!

00:23:15.270 --> 00:23:16.080
There we go.

00:23:18.450 --> 00:23:19.680
There.

00:23:21.970 --> 00:23:25.060
What, exactly, are we watching here?

00:23:27.260 --> 00:23:28.630
I can't catch any!

00:23:28.630 --> 00:23:31.340
Your Highness, more are falling!

00:23:32.240 --> 00:23:34.510
Well, it's heart-warming, so it's fine.

00:23:34.510 --> 00:23:36.020
And we get to drink for free.

00:23:36.020 --> 00:23:37.360
Yep.
